    }
  ],
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The total number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> hybridised carbon atoms in the major product <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">P</mi></math> (a non-heterocyclic compound) of the following reaction is</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/973162f4-76d6-4624-a757-93a1a93048c4.png\" style=\"width: 429px; height: 94px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "28",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Lithium aluminium hydride is a strong reducing agent. It reduces cyanide to primary amine with no loss of carbon. Primary amine can undergo nucleophilic addition reaction with acetophenone to produce imine derivative. The carbon with one pi bond are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridised carbon. All the carbon in benzene ring are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridised. Hence, totally 28&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;carbon are present in the molecule.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/01aa90e1-603a-4f09-b202-0196bd6b0522.png\" style=\"width: 559px; height: 419px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
